  "summary": "A vacuum relief valve protects a tank or vessel from collapsing under vacuum — for example when it is emptied quickly or when hot vapour condenses. When the internal pressure falls below the set vacuum, atmospheric pressure pushes the pallet open against its spring and air flows in; when the pressures equalise the spring closes it.",
